    "reason": "The linked PR [ev-cf897316507c] explains the release-note title [ev-b0185d1375a7]. Crossplane now checks that each composed resource returned by a composition function has a valid Kubernetes resource name. This stops `resourceRefs` from being filled with an invalid name, which used to happen because the refs are written before the resource is applied. That roughly covers applicability: XRs whose function pipeline returns composed resources with invalid names. It does not state the consequence: what the controller does when validation fails (fail the whole XR reconcile, skip only that resource, or report it through a condition or event), or what happens to refs that are already invalid. The changed-file list [ev-958a98c1c27d] doesn't show this behaviour, and the linked issue #6534 that would describe the original failure isn't in the evidence.",
